# This file now governs BOTH images, because expense-ledger/Dockerfile also
# builds from the repo root (it has to reach packages/shared). Docker matches
# these patterns against the full path from the context root, so the bare
# entries above only cover the root level — the nested equivalents have to be
# spelled out or expense-ledger/node_modules ships into the build context.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
